  "note": "The Portal's answers to reports (Auth/Portal, 2026-11-10). 200 confirms; a network error, a timeout, a 5xx, a 429 (after its Retry-After) or a 401 (after refreshing the station.report token) is retried with the same report_id and body; a final refusal (400, 404, 409 report_id_reused or invalid_state, 413, 415, any other 4xx) settles the report with an operator alert, and the reports waiting for it go once the others are settled; a 403 settles every report and stops reporting, with one alert, while counting goes on. Here host-b's report is confirmed after a 401; host-c's is refused for good (409); the deadline's revoked{deadline_passed} waits for neither once both are settled, is retried after a 503 and a 429, and then gets a 403: reporting stops, and host-d applying the revocation later makes no report. A restart keeps the stop.",
